menu "WireGuard crypto (wireguard_lwip)"

    config WG_CRYPTO_IRAM
        bool "Run ChaCha20-Poly1305 from IRAM"
        default n
        help
            Place the per-packet ChaCha20/Poly1305 code (about 5 KB) in IRAM instead of
            flash. Flash code runs through the instruction cache, which Wi-Fi and the
            TCP/IP stack share; if they evict the cipher's loops between packets every
            packet pays cache refills. Costs IRAM, which is scarce on this firmware:
            enable only if `crypto bench` shows "avg" well above "min".

    config WG_CRYPTO_BENCH_BASELINE
        bool "Include the original ChaCha20-Poly1305 in `crypto bench` for A/B comparison"
        default n
        help
            Links the pre-optimisation implementation (crypto/legacy) and prints its
            timings next to the optimised code. Diagnostics only; adds about 4 KB of flash.

endmenu
